, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765600, "segment_id": "5CWbDAxkjF", "segment_broadcast_id": "NYV2HfGxPn", "segment_title": "North Korea / Nuclear Tests", "segment_description": "(Studio: Terry Moran)  Report introduced. \n (White House: Geoff Morrell)  The mystery surrounding an explosion in North Korea that might have been a nuclear test examined.  [On \"Meet the Press,\" Secretary of State Colin POWELL; National Security Advisor Condoleezza RICE&#134;- say North Korea has not conducted tests.]  [Former ambassador to South Korea Donald GREGG&#134;- assesses the situation in North Korea.]  Statement from Senator John Kerry about President Bush & North Korea's nuclear program quoted.", "segment_duration": 110, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "810.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765605, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "NYV2HfGxPn", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-12", "broadcast_start_time": "0.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765600, "segment_id": "ofdckON3N2", "segment_broadcast_id": "NYV2HfGxPn", "segment_title": "Middle East / Israeli Settlements / Sharon", "segment_description": "(Studio: Terry Moran)  Protests in Jerusalem against Israeli Prime Minister Ariel Sharon's plan to close settlements in the occupied territories shown. \n (Jerusalem: Dean Reynolds)  The threats against Sharon's life from militant Jewish settlers featured; scenes shown of unrest; details recalled of the 1995 murder of Prime Minister Yitzhak Rabin & of the view that the Gaza land is a heavenly gift to the Jewish people.  [Hebrew University Abraham DISKIN&#134;- says we cannot tolerate this.]  [Activist Baruch MARZEL&#134;- comments.]", "segment_d